WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.170
- So you got married and
became a mom in your 40s,

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.610
which I think is amazing

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.550
because I didn't start to
do anything really until 31,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.383
I feel like,

00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:11.220
and I feel like I really had a life.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.710
I feel like I had like my selfish years,

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.210
I feel like I wasn't ready.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.530
Like, is there a reason why
you waited so long to do it?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.830
- Yeah (she laughs)

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.780
- I saw those eyes.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.613
- You're so sweet.

00:00:19.613 --> 00:00:21.260
You're like, I mean, I was 31.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.580
I was 41 when I got
married and had a baby.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.690
- Where I'm from, you're
basically dead at 31,

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.850
like I'm from the south.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.740
So yeah, people are like, "Oh,
so you're gonna die alone."

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.020
Like, so by 30, yeah,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:33.853
that was a

00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:34.686
big deal.
- That's so antiquated,

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:35.519
isn't it?
- Yes,

00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:36.770
that's why I don't, I love,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.070
I loved having my 20s.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.471
I loved figuring some stuff out

00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:42.323
and it turns out I needed
to figure some more out.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.070
- I just, for me, I think
everyone's different obviously,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.163
but for me,

00:00:47.532 --> 00:00:49.713
and I talk about this a lot in the book.

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:52.553
I didn't have a great example of marriage.

00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:55.470
My parents divorced when I was a year old

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.873
and I didn't have the
most stable upbringing.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:02.720
I had a lot of love and,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.380
but I never felt like I had
a good example of marriage.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.260
So why would I?

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.280
That was one reason.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.370
And the other reason was
honestly, I never met,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.500
I wasn't,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.790
for me, it took me a long time
to get rid of my narrative

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.670
of what marriage was

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.640
and picking the wrong people,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.720
which is why I never
felt like getting married

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.260
because I just couldn't imagine
a life with that person.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.790
And then when I met,
when I met my husband,

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.370
it was six months in to
us dating when I thought,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.540
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.840
- [Guest] Aw, there he is!

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.890
- [Kelly] Six months in?

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:37.723
- [Guest] Six months in

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:39.470
I thought if he asked me to
marry him tomorrow, I would.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.370
I mean, at that point I
was 39 when I met him.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.230
And I just, it was like, yeah, I would.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.100
He didn't.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.880
I mean, he waited a year and a bit.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:48.713
Yeah.

00:01:48.713 --> 00:01:49.970
But, but yeah.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.580
Once, I just knew, I was like,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.640
life is so easy with him.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.653
Everything's easy and
more fun and it felt good.

00:01:57.653 --> 00:02:01.120
And then, you know, and I said to him,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.570
I actually did say this to him.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.320
He's six years younger than I am.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.640
And I said, listen, you are,

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.680
he comes from a really good family,

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.420
and really good family values.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.310
And his parents have a
healthy, happy marriage.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:16.130
And I said, you know, I'm turning,

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:17.210
I was about to turn 40,

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.900
and I said, I think maybe you should,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.810
we should probably break up

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.300
so you can go and find a girl.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.540
I don't know if I can have kids.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.360
I don't even know if I want them.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.330
And you're a family guy

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.260
and I can see how
important family is to you.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.260
And he just laughed at me.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.754
He was like,

00:02:31.754 --> 00:02:33.730
I think it's more important
to find the person

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.060
you want to spend your life
with and the rest will follow.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.580
- And he's probably like, I
think I'll make the choice.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.850
- Yeah, and I was really
impressed with that

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.330
because so many guys seem,

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.990
you know, age seems like
a big deal to us women,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.120
especially when you hit 40 and
you haven't had a child yet.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.570
There's this strange thing
that society does to us,

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.040
which is like, you're
washed up or it's over.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.850
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And that's just,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.544
that's just not true.

00:02:55.544 --> 00:02:57.720
And I wouldn't have
been ready to have a kid

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.480
or have a marriage until I was 40.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.130
I just wasn't ready.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.420
And now I'm grateful that,
I mean, I got really lucky.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.863
We got pregnant by accident,
totally by accident,

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:13.130
without knowing, just before
he asked me to marry him.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.130
But it was just a happy coincidence.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.730
And I thank the lucky stars cause I,

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.898
I am not the same person, you know,

00:03:20.898 --> 00:03:24.580
at 30 that I would have been at 40.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.920
And so I had the time.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.680
And also like you said,
I've been there, done that.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.110
I don't want, I love having
an excuse to stay home

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.860
and not have to go to the party.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.383
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, I'm her.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.630
- Sorry, I don't have a babysitter.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.810
- And it's not that I'm being snobby

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.520
or like I'm, you know, I'm a recluse.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.400
I just really, I feel like
I did a lot of things.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.420
Like in my twenties, I traveled,
I did all of the things.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.130
I feel like if you get
married before that,

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.520
there might be end up
being a level of resentment

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.260
that you didn't, you
missed out on something.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.710
Or I don't know, I felt that.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.850
That's why I didn't, I didn't get married.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.330
I think a lot of people feel that way

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.700
and they have children way too young.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.100
And then it causes problems,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.100
but I felt like I was at the
perfect time to have a baby.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.530
I was ready.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.780
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

